788	// decision and the first that does not invent a discriminator, so the four
789	// refused rules are recorded here to stop a sixth from re-deriving one.
790	// Measurements are against a 939-file ground-truth corpus (674 images / 265
791	// text files, every image decode-checked twice — Pillow `open`+`load` and
792	// giflib `DGifOpenFileName`+`DGifSlurp`), plus 138 later counterexamples built
793	// specifically to break whichever rule was current.
794	//
795	//   * `false` ("inconclusive means text", round 2): refuses all 92 corpus
796	//     images that open on an outrunning comment; 88 become 3,063 prose records.
797	//   * `seen > 1 && every size seen is 0xFF` (round 3), on the reasoning that
798	//     encoders pack long comments maximally. They do not. giflib's streaming
799	//     `EGifPutExtensionBlock` writes ONE sub-block per call at whatever length
800	//     the caller passed, so chains of 1, 2, 16, 32, 64, 100, 120, 127, 128,

1601	            }
1602	        }
1603	    }
1604	    fields.push(cur);
